{
  "id": "safe",
  "label": "Safe",
  "icon": "shield",
  "description": "Safe harbour: everything heavy down, power saver, minimal CPU state. A real Safe Mode boot needs bcdedit safeboot and a reboot -- see docs/RUNSTATES.md before enabling that.",
  "est_seconds": 45,
  "x_notes": "Live safe state only. Reboot-class safe mode (bcdedit /set {current} safeboot minimal) is documented but deliberately NOT in this manifest: an engine step cannot un-apply it without a second reboot, so it stays a human decision.",
